;;; `owed-seats.ein` with **Ann renamed Zed**, and nothing else — the twin that
;;; makes M1e2 **W5** an order dependence rather than only a wrong count.
;;; Register row `W5/owed-seats`, as a twin.
;;;
;;; The lattice answers k = 3 here too, but its third model is
;;; `{(seats Bob C1), (seats Bob C2), (seats Zed C1)}` — mapped back, Bob on
;;; both chairs and Ann on C1, where the original file's third model put **Ann**
;;; on both chairs. Renaming a constant changes which superset the name-sorted
;;; prefix join builds, so it changes the model set. A model set that moves
;;; under a renaming is wrong under every reading of Q-M1e2.1.
;;;
;;; Banked from M1e2's probes at S1e2.1.1.
(import std.algebra :symbols (total-owed surjective-owed))
(relation is-a   T T)
(relation seats  Guest Chair)
(is-a Zed Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(is-a C1 Chair)  (is-a C2 Chair)
(total-owed      seats is-a)
(surjective-owed seats is-a)
(query :goal (seats ?g ?c))
